-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/885203-why-aren-t-there-horrors-of-things-other-than-fears?p=902066#post902066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Undertale. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed, but <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monsters,_Inc.\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Monsters Inc</b></a> still has a special place in my heart.<br /> <br /> To answer the question in the thread's title...well, it's right there in their name. If there are super-Goetia embodying other primal aspects of the human psyche, they should be called something else. Who knows, maybe the source of Inspiration from Genius: The Transgression is located somewhere in a Temenos Realm that is close to the Anima Mundi, but not as close as the Primordial Dream. Our desire to discover, comprehend and invent definitely came after the basic impulses of fear and hunger. That desire may not be primordial in the strictest sense, but I think it is still a defining characteristic of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:15:09-07:00","id":902157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div